<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:04Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Guinea's gold rush: Arrests, deportations spark outcry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee1f9da65bb2c30ebb2afd47664bf4dac2cae0d2435c600cb2c78cc2850ecd1e</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-s-gold-rush-arrests-deportations-spark-outcry/a-79922842--da7e32f94527.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-s-gold-rush-arrests-deportations-spark-outcry/a-79922842?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Guinea has banned illegal gold mining, citing environmental concerns. It has further charged hundreds of suspected local and foreign illegal miners amid reports of rights abuses and deportations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany joins 4 other EU states to set up Rwanda deportation hub</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9aa2ce5266d6575b97f4583f1da19dc4395b7e268d4c1535ee3aa58dd1baddea</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T12:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-joins-4-other-eu-states-to-set-up-rwanda-deportation-hub/a-79959158--227aa9c95b79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-joins-4-other-eu-states-to-set-up-rwanda-deportation-hub/a-79959158?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The move follows approval of EU regulations that ease deportations and allow hubs to be set up outside the bloc. A similar scheme by the UK government fell apart over legal issues though the US has one up and running.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa: 17 killed in separate mass shooting incidents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f183cd348ff7cf119efbc1e7e03c1e71bae00e4172ca357a5c4795ecd9c4274e</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T10:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-17-killed-in-separate-mass-shooting-incidents/a-79956966--4668c90e6459.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-17-killed-in-separate-mass-shooting-incidents/a-79956966?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police are investigating two mass shooting incidents in Gauteng and KwaZulu-Natal provinces. There has been a growing trend of mass shooting incidents making headlines in recent years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nearly 1,600 migrants arrive on Spain's Canary Islands in one day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d8f63803415ac25da71dfba4a0462383f453c9787c28fe36a7d00bb9e2423be</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T18:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nearly-1-600-migrants-arrive-on-spain-s-canary-islands-in-one-day/a-79952941--709bffa2c1cc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nearly-1-600-migrants-arrive-on-spain-s-canary-islands-in-one-day/a-79952941?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The majority of the migrants who arrived on the islands on Saturday came from Senegal, Gambia, and Guinea. The surge in arrivals to the Canaries comes after Spain's Ceuta recently faced a migration crisis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:229044eb65f29fe020e51c060c2c09d06a6ce00955bf9d10d2d64b446e7d10e6</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
